.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/tslib Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "tslib"
.PP
This is a runtime library for \fRTypeScript\fP that contains all of the TypeScript helper functions\&.

.PP
This library is primarily used by the \fR--importHelpers\fP flag in TypeScript\&. When using \fR--importHelpers\fP, a module that uses helper functions like \fR__extends\fP and \fR__assign\fP in the following emitted file:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var __assign = (this && this\&.__assign) || Object\&.assign || function(t) {
    for (var s, i = 1, n = arguments\&.length; i < n; i++) {
        s = arguments[i];
        for (var p in s) if (Object\&.prototype\&.hasOwnProperty\&.call(s, p))
            t[p] = s[p];
    }
    return t;
};
exports\&.x = {};
exports\&.y = __assign({}, exports\&.x);
.fi
.PP

.PP
will instead be emitted as something like the following:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var tslib_1 = require("tslib");
exports\&.x = {};
exports\&.y = tslib_1\&.__assign({}, exports\&.x);
.fi
.PP

.PP
Because this can avoid duplicate declarations of things like \fR__extends\fP, \fR__assign\fP, etc\&., this means delivering users smaller files on average, as well as less runtime overhead\&. For optimized bundles with TypeScript, you should absolutely consider using \fRtslib\fP and \fR--importHelpers\fP\&.
.SH "Installing"
.PP
For the latest stable version, run:
.SS "npm"
.PP
.nf
# TypeScript 3\&.9\&.2 or later
npm install tslib

# TypeScript 3\&.8\&.4 or earlier
npm install tslib@^1

# TypeScript 2\&.3\&.2 or earlier
npm install tslib@1\&.6\&.1
.fi
.PP
.SS "yarn"
.PP
.nf
# TypeScript 3\&.9\&.2 or later
yarn add tslib

# TypeScript 3\&.8\&.4 or earlier
yarn add tslib@^1

# TypeScript 2\&.3\&.2 or earlier
yarn add tslib@1\&.6\&.1
.fi
.PP
.SS "bower"
.PP
.nf
# TypeScript 3\&.9\&.2 or later
bower install tslib

# TypeScript 3\&.8\&.4 or earlier
bower install tslib@^1

# TypeScript 2\&.3\&.2 or earlier
bower install tslib@1\&.6\&.1
.fi
.PP
.SS "JSPM"
.PP
.nf
# TypeScript 3\&.9\&.2 or later
jspm install tslib

# TypeScript 3\&.8\&.4 or earlier
jspm install tslib@^1

# TypeScript 2\&.3\&.2 or earlier
jspm install tslib@1\&.6\&.1
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Set the \fRimportHelpers\fP compiler option on the command line:

.PP
.PP
.nf
tsc \-\-importHelpers file\&.ts
.fi
.PP

.PP
or in your tsconfig\&.json:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    "compilerOptions": {
        "importHelpers": true
    }
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "For bower and JSPM users"
You will need to add a \fRpaths\fP mapping for \fRtslib\fP, e\&.g\&. For Bower users:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    "compilerOptions": {
        "module": "amd",
        "importHelpers": true,
        "baseUrl": "\&./",
        "paths": {
            "tslib" : ["bower_components/tslib/tslib\&.d\&.ts"]
        }
    }
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
For JSPM users:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    "compilerOptions": {
        "module": "system",
        "importHelpers": true,
        "baseUrl": "\&./",
        "paths": {
            "tslib" : ["jspm_packages/npm/tslib@2\&.x\&.y/tslib\&.d\&.ts"]
        }
    }
}
.fi
.PP
